    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Because you're growing! Your mouth and jaw get bigger, but your baby teeth stay small.",
      "punch": "growing",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "📏",
        "text": "You're growing!",
        "cue": "growing",
        "sub": "Your jaw gets bigger",
        "sub_cue": "jaw"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "So small teeth don't fit anymore?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Right! A grown-up mouth needs bigger teeth. And they're already waiting in your gums, under your baby teeth.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🦷",
        "text": "Big teeth wait below",
        "cue": "waiting",
        "sub": "Hiding in your gums",
        "sub_cue": "gums"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Wait, there are teeth hiding in there right now?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Yep! A big tooth pushes up, and the baby tooth's roots slowly melt away. So it gets wiggly and falls out.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "Tooth swap",
        "traveler": "🦷",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "⬆️",
            "label": "Big tooth up",
            "cue": "pushes"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✨",
            "label": "Roots melt",
            "cue": "roots"
          },
          {
            "icon": "〰️",
            "label": "Gets wiggly",
            "cue": "wiggly"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⬇️",
            "label": "Falls out",
            "cue": "falls"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Usually just a little. And the new tooth soon grows in to fill the gap.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "😁",
        "text": "The new tooth fills the gap",
        "cue": "gap",
        "sub": "Just a little wait",
        "sub_cue": "grows"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "LEO",
      "text": "How many baby teeth do I have?"
    },
    {
      "who": "MIA",
      "text": "Most kids have twenty baby teeth. Grown-ups can end up with thirty-two big teeth!",
      "punch": "twenty",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "Kids",
          "items": [
            {
